'''Visakhapatnam district'''<ref>{{Cite book|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=ZELmNAkC8R0C&q=Vizagapatnam+District&pg=PA277|title=Raj to Swaraj: A Textbook on Colonialism and Nationalism in India|last=Pradhāna|first=Rāmacandra|date=2008|publisher=Macmillan India|isbn=978-0-230-63406-0|language=en}}</ref> is a  district in the [[Uttarandhra]] region of the [[States and union territories of India|Indian state]] of [[Andhra Pradesh]], headquartered at [[Visakhapatnam]].<ref name="census2011">{{cite web |title=District Census Hand Book – Visakhapatnam |url=https://censusindia.gov.in/nada/index.php/catalog/122/download/138/DH_2011_2813_PART_A_DCHB_VISAKHAPATNAM.pdf|website=[[Census of India]] |publisher=[[Registrar General and Census Commissioner of India]]}}</ref>{{Rp|14}} It is one of the twenty-six [[List of districts of Andhra Pradesh|districts in Andhra Pradesh]] state. The district shares borders with [[Vizianagaram district]] in north and south-east and with [[Anakapalli district]] in the  south-west and [[Bay of Bengal]] in the south.<ref name="map">{{cite web|url=http://www.censusindia.gov.in/2011census/dchb/2813_PART_A_DCHB_VISAKHAPATNAM.pdf|title=District Census Hand Book : Visakhapatnam (Part A)|date=2011|website=[[Census of India]]|publisher=Directorate of Census Operations, Andhra Pradesh|access-date=1 June 2019}}</ref>{{Rp|15}}

== History ==
During the [[British Raj|British rule in India]], Visakhapatnam emerged as a district in the year 1802. Chicacole (present-day [[Srikakulam]]) which was in Visakhapatnam district was incorporated into Ganjam when the latter was formed as a district.<ref>{{Cite web|date=30 March 2022|title=AP new districts: First formed under the empire, Andhra Pradesh's map shaped and reshaped over centuries|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/visakhapatnam/first-formed-under-the-empire-aps-map-shaped-and-reshaped-over-two-centuries/articleshow/90528597.cms|access-date=2 April 2022|website=[[The Times of India]]|language=en}}</ref> On 1 April 1936, Bihar and Orissa Province was split to form [[Bihar Province]] and [[Orissa Province]]. Parts of the [[Vizagapatam district (Madras Presidency)|Vizagapatam district]] (i.e., [[Nabarangpur]], [[Malkangiri]], [[Koraput]], [[Jeypore]], [[Rayagada]] etc.) and the [[Ganjam District (Madras Presidency)|Ganjam district]] (excluding Chicacole division) of [[Madras Presidency]] were transferred to [[Orissa Province]] along with portions of the [[Vizagapatam Hill Tracts Agency]] and [[Ganjam Hill Tracts Agency]].<ref>[https://www.worldstatesmen.org/India_BrProvinces.htm Provinces of British India]</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=The Untouchables|url=https://knappily.com/Features/april-1-1936-odisha-comes-into-being/5ac13b6f5c96e8f11b0cfa78|publisher=Siddharth Books & Google ebooks|date=1948|access-date=2 April 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite book|title=April 1,1936: Odisha comes into being|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=iH2nqo7ADeUC&dq=vizagapatam+and+ganjam+areas+tranferred+to+orissa+province&pg=PA35|publisher=Knappilly|date=1 April 2018|isbn = 978-81-905689-2-0|access-date=2 April 2022}}</ref> The Chicacole division (i.e., [[Ichchapuram]], [[Palasa]], [[Tekkali]], [[Pathapatnam]] and [[Srikakulam]]) was merged with Visakhapatnam district.

Later, in 1950, [[Srikakulam district]] was carved out from the erstwhile Visakhapatnam district.<ref>{{Cite web|title=District level information of Srikakulam|url=https://www.indiastatdistricts.com/andhrapradesh/srikakulam-district|access-date=11 October 2022|website=Districts of India|language=en}}</ref> In 1979, part of the district was split to form [[Vizianagaram district]].<ref name="Statoids">{{cite web|last=Law|first=Gwillim|date=25 September 2011|title=Districts of India|url=https://www.statoids.com/yin.html|access-date=11 October 2011|work=Statoids}}</ref> Visakhapatnam district is currently a part of the [[Red corridor]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://intellibriefs.blogspot.com/2009/12/naxal-menace-83-districts-under.html |title=83 districts under the Security Related Expenditure Scheme |publisher=IntelliBriefs |date=11 December 2009 |access-date=17 September 2011 |archive-date=27 October 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111027115807/http://intellibriefs.blogspot.com/2009/12/naxal-menace-83-districts-under.html |url-status=dead }}</ref>

On 3 April 2022, [[Government of Andhra Pradesh]] created 13 new districts in the state, hence the district was once again divided into three i.e., Visakhapatnam, [[Anakapalli district|Anakapalli]] and [[Alluri Sitharama Raju district|Alluri Sitharama Raju]] districts. This made Vizag the only district with 90% urban population in AP.
===Historical demographics===
{{historical populations|11=1901|12=9,92,833|13=1911|14=10,56,683|15=1921|16=10,57,223|17=1931|18=11,75,984|19=1941|20=13,14,362|21=1951|22=14,83,653|23=1961|24=16,65,213|25=1971|26=20,35,831|27=1981|28=25,76,474|29=1991|30=32,85,092|31=2001|32=38,32,336|33=2011|34=42,90,589|percentages=pagr|footnote=source:<ref>[http://www.censusindia.gov.in/2011census/PCA/A2_Data_Table.html Decadal Variation In Population Since 1901]</ref>|align=right}}According to the [[2011 Census of India|2011 census]] Visakhapatnam district has a [[Demographics of India|population]] of 4,290,589. This gives it a ranking of 44 in India (out of a total of [[List of districts in India|640 districts]]) and fourth in the state. The district has a population density of {{convert| 384 |PD/sqkm|PD/sqmi}}. Its [[Family planning in India|population growth rate]] over the decade 2001–2011 was 11.89%. It has a [[Human sex ratio|sex ratio]] of 1003 [[Women in India|females]] for every 1000 males, and a [[Literacy in India|literacy rate]] of 67.7%.

